# Project Layer

This file is **stamped at provisioning time** by the provisioning system that created this repo (typically an internal portal with SSO). It is the single source of truth for who owns this project and what deployment layer it sits at. IT reads this file when reviewing promotion requests.

**Filename rule:** the provisioning system replaces every `<<intake:...>>` token below and renames the file from `LAYER.md.template` → `LAYER.md`. The `.template` suffix is the visible marker that stamping has not yet happened. If you are reading this file at `LAYER.md.template`, the provisioning step did not run — fix that before doing anything else.

If you cloned this template directly without going through the provisioning system, fill the tokens by hand and rename the file. Do not delete it.

